.TH SCREENCAPTURE 1 "November 2026" "screencapture 1.0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
screencapture \- lightweight X11 screenshot tool (SimpleScreenShot)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B screencapture
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B screencapture
captures screen regions on X11 desktops (GTK3 frontend). By default it
starts a system tray icon and immediately opens a full-screen capture
overlay: drag to select a region, then annotate (arrow, rectangle,
ellipse, line, text, mosaic, step numbering), pin the result to the
desktop, copy it to the clipboard, save it, stitch a long screenshot,
scan QR codes, run OCR text recognition or record the screen to a
video.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-quit
One-shot mode: open the capture overlay without the tray icon and exit
the application once the capture window is closed.
.TP
.BI \-\-enter\  mode
Startup mode. Use
.B tray
to start minimized to the system tray without opening a capture
overlay.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang\  code
UI language override; for example
.BR zh\-CN ", " en\-US ", " zh\-TW ", " ja\-JP ", " ru\-RU " or " id\-ID .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/simplescreenshot/assets/
System-installed runtime resources (icon font, logo, translations).
.TP
.I ~/.config/screencapture/
Per-user configuration and data (config.json).
.SH NOTES
Optional features rely on helper programs shipped as package
recommends; each feature checks its helper when used and shows a
missing-dependency dialog instead of failing silently. Screen
recording (MP4/GIF, optionally with system audio and microphone
captured through PipeWire or PulseAudio) needs
.BR ffmpeg (1).
OCR needs
.BR tesseract (1)
with the desired language packs (recommended:
.IR tesseract\-ocr\-chi\-sim ).
Images are also persisted through
.BR xclip (1)
when no clipboard manager is running. QR code decoding has no external
dependency (the quirc decoder is bundled).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR xclip (1)
